{"title":"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is the perpendicular bisector of chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, intersecting it in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. \nBetween <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> is taken, \nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643076c7d3dbf3403cff81e7736208fb5312cfbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EU$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> extended meets the circle in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Then, for any selection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, as described, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed9ac97c9609a7f34286c9ac01c28e7c6c5d155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EUM$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> is similar to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a52512780abab0cb8d6d4a50f8c3bb3d4f5c5d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair B = (-0.866, -0.5); pair C = (0.866, -0.5); pair E = (0, -1); pair F = (0, 1); pair M = midpoint(B--C); pair A = (-0.99, -0.141); pair U = intersectionpoints(A--E, B--C)[0]; draw(B--C); draw(F--E--A); draw(unitcircle); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, S); label(&quot;$U$&quot;, U, NE); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, NE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, N); //Credit to MSTang for the asymptote[/asy]\" width=\"238\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c1dc007a3a41897056034c394d98aeb2ef2a0ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\triangle EFA \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\triangle EFC \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\triangle ABM \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\triangle ABU \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\triangle FMC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"608\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed9ac97c9609a7f34286c9ac01c28e7c6c5d155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EUM$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangle</a> with one of the angles being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/c/2ccb4cf0fc8da6d8a5d7527911f005ca9daab2de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FEA$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />.  This leads to prediction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca293a0e8fb27e47ca1998d57119ab8eb386a6f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle FEA$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is the similar triangle as it shares an angle, and to prove this, we need to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is a diameter.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/57792c54ac030b7603c2ec409a282015525c0b4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair B = (-0.866, -0.5); pair C = (0.866, -0.5); pair E = (0, -1); pair F = (0, 1); pair M = midpoint(B--C); pair A = (-0.99, -0.141); pair U = intersectionpoints(A--E, B--C)[0]; draw(B--C); draw(F--E--A); draw(unitcircle); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, S); label(&quot;$U$&quot;, U, NE); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, NE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, N); draw(&quot;$D$&quot;,(0,0),NE); draw(B--(0,0)--C,dotted); draw(F--A); dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot((0,0)); dot(E); dot(F); dot(U); dot(M); //Credit to MSTang for the asymptote[/asy]\" width=\"238\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a15f3239cf7dc2bd672e7a72a1278ccf1bfbd88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD = DB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />, then by SAS Congruency, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d3a2172063fe8805e810592d25aed7fdd74fdf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DMB \\cong \\triangle DMC$\" width=\"155\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/c/f5c4a23a16cef37c145bd6100600604e7030ec94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD = DB = DC$\" width=\"138\" height=\"12\" />.  Since three points define a circle and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is equidistant from three points, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the center, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is a diameter.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/008f83a32c6ef6e3c213bb8abe94874de03340f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EAF$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> is a right angle, and by AA Similarity, we can confirm that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/b/83b56199ba7040481e91336ff8c7938dfa090082.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EFA \\sim \\triangle EUM$\" width=\"147\" height=\"13\" />.  The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME\" title=\"1963 AHSME\">1963 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1963 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1963\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1963 AHSME Pr